    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (83.21) stands as our premier offensive anchor. His favorable matchup against Rogers in a high-park-factor environment, combined with the stolen base upside afforded by the opposing pitcher's slow delivery time, makes him an elite play. **Bryce Harper** (79.53) also projects exceptionally well, benefiting from a soft matchup against Holmes and the inherent stability of the #3 spot in the lineup. **Luis Arraez** (69.53) remains a high-floor start today; the pairing of his elite contact skills against the vulnerable Holmes creates a strong buffer for our daily batting average target.\n\nWe are leaning into favorable park and platoon matchups elsewhere, specifically with **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.45), whose score is buoyed by a beneficial wind forecast, and **Justin Crawford** (64.45). Despite the #9 spot in the order, **Justin Crawford** remains essential to our roster strategy given our league\u2019s aggressive prioritization of speed; he is the primary engine for our stolen base production today. Conversely, **Gleyber Torres** (41.16) and **JJ Bleday** (41.25) sit near the bottom of our active lineup, both suffering from poor SP matchups and platoon disadvantages that keep them barely above our 40.0 efficiency floor. \n\nOur most difficult decision occurred at the bench, where **Alex Freeland** (38.59) narrowly missed the cut. While he possesses some versatility as a switch-hitter, the combination of a tough matchup against Burns and his placement in the #9 slot suppressed his raw projection below our \"Strong\" tier. We opted to prioritize the higher-upside profiles of our starters to maximize our chances in the counting categories. Please note the status of **Tyler Freeman**, who remains in the minors, and **Will Smith** and **Cal Raleigh**, who are unavailable today; ensure our lineup integrity is maintained despite these specific availability constraints.",
